# Docker-First Development

This project runs entirely in Docker. **Never run `pnpm`, `npm`, `node`, `prisma`, `nest`, or `next` directly on the host** unless the user explicitly asks for a host-only workflow.

## Containers

| Service | Container name | Port | Working dir |
|---------|----------------|------|-------------|
| PostgreSQL | `calendar_db` | 5432 | — |
| NestJS API | `calendar_api` | 3001 | `/app` |
| Next.js web | `calendar_web` | 3000 | `/app` |

## Command pattern

Run commands from the **repository root** on the host:

```bash
docker compose exec api <command>      # backend, prisma, monorepo scripts
docker compose exec web <command>      # frontend scripts
docker compose exec db <command>       # postgres CLI (psql)
```

Examples:

```bash
docker compose exec api pnpm install
docker compose exec api pnpm prisma generate --schema=./packages/database/prisma/schema.prisma
docker compose exec api pnpm --filter api test
docker compose exec web pnpm --filter web lint
```

## Lifecycle (host)

```bash
docker compose watch                 # preferred dev mode: start + file watch (foreground)
docker compose up --watch            # alternative: start with watch in foreground
docker compose up -d                 # start detached (no compose watch; bind mounts still work)
docker compose logs -f api           # follow API logs
docker compose up -d --build api web # rebuild after dependency changes
docker compose down                  # stop all services
```

## Docker Compose Watch

`docker-compose.yml` defines `develop.watch` for `api` and `web`. Use watch mode during active development:

| Action | Triggered by | Effect |
|--------|--------------|--------|
| `sync` | Source file edits | Copies changed files into the container (no rebuild) |
| `rebuild` | Dependency/config changes | Rebuilds the service image and restarts the container |

**API** — sync: `apps/api/` (ignores `node_modules/`, `dist/`), `packages/` · rebuild: `package.json`, `apps/api/package.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`

**Web** — sync: `apps/web/` (ignores `node_modules/`, `.next/`) · rebuild: `package.json`, `apps/web/package.json`, `tailwind.config.ts`, `next.config.mjs`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`

NestJS (`nest --watch`) and Next.js (`next dev`) hot-reload inside containers. Polling is enabled (`CHOKIDAR_USEPOLLING`, `CHOKIDAR_INTERVAL=300`, `WATCHPACK_POLLING`) for reliable file detection on Windows. Use `docker compose watch` (not plain `up -d`) so `develop.watch` sync rules are active.

## Rules

1. Prefer `docker compose watch` for day-to-day development; use `docker compose up -d` only when watch is not needed.
2. Use `api` container for Prisma, tests, lint, and any monorepo-wide `pnpm` command.
3. Use `web` container only for frontend-specific commands when isolation matters; most `pnpm --filter` commands work from `api` too.
4. Inside containers, `DATABASE_URL` points to host `db` (not `localhost`).
5. After changing `package.json` or `pnpm-lock.yaml`, watch triggers rebuild automatically; otherwise run `docker compose up -d --build`.
